157
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:13,380
Alright, so one of the great words that we heard in today's dialogue was exotic.

158
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:20,120
This is not necessarily describing a person, but usually things or clothes or places.

159
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:23,380
In this instance, it was some place exotic.

160
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,420
What's an exotic place?

161
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:34,680
It's basically a place that's very unique and I guess it's kind of not common to go there or to find.

162
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:40,800
For example, many people talk about an exotic getaway going to the jungle because it's so exotic.

163
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:44,240
You have so many strange animals and plants and everything is so unfamiliar.

164
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:55,540
Right, so in my mind, Tahiti is very exotic. It's full of jungle and there's also beaches and it's very unusual for someone who's from America because it's just so far away.

165
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,980
That's right, exotic.

166
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:05,360
So, someone can also have an exotic personality because maybe they're a little bit strange or not strange but not so common, maybe unique.

167
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:10,320
Yeah, although exotic is usually kind of a sexy thing when you're talking about people.

168
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:14,600
You know, she looks very exotic. That means she doesn't look like everybody else here.

169
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:15,340
That's right.

170
